{"type":"standard","title":"Kimba language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kimba language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3914404","titles":{"canonical":"Kimba_language","normalized":"Kimba language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kimba language</span></span>"},"pageid":33487584,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1327867068","tid":"3ef76b48-da91-11f0-ab56-14e2fc1f869b","timestamp":"2025-12-16T15:09:41Z","description":"Kainji language group of Nigeria","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimba_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimba_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimba_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kimba_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimba_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Kimba_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimba_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kimba_language"}},"extract":"The Kimba languages (Tsikimba or the Kambari II languages) are a group of Kainji languages of Nigeria spoken by the Kambari people. The languages are Kimba (Tsikimba), Gaushi (Agaushi), and Wenci (Ngwunci).","extract_html":"<p>The <b>Kimba languages</b> (<b>Tsikimba</b> or the <b>Kambari II languages</b>) are a group of Kainji languages of Nigeria spoken by the Kambari people. The languages are <b>Kimba (Tsikimba)</b>, Gaushi (Agaushi), and Wenci (Ngwunci).</p>"}